WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.464
Host: Give a receptor-to-response explanation
of slowing at the sinoatrial node.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:14.137
Guide: Acetylcholine activates cardiac M2
receptors. Gi/o signalling reduces cyclic AMP,

3
00:00:14.137 --> 00:00:19.800
Guide: while beta–gamma subunits can activate
GIRK potassium channels.

4
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.384
Guide: These changes reduce pacemaker activity
and slow the heart.

5
00:00:24.384 --> 00:00:33.107
Host: A learner says every sympathetic
postganglionic neuron releases noradrenaline.
Which example corrects the claim?

6
00:00:33.107 --> 00:00:38.126
Guide: Sympathetic fibres to eccrine sweat
glands release acetylcholine.

7
00:00:38.126 --> 00:00:43.729
Guide: Eccrine sweat-gland innervation is the
important sympathetic cholinergic exception.
